  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "## Next\n\n- Ships the DbProvider code rules (`DbProviderRules`, IDs `RJIT_CR_DBP_00001`-`00006`) inside this package: register them in a code rule project with `AddRulePack<DbProviderRules>()`. They keep data access on the query provider: no Dapper, one query provider per method, always created with `using`, no `IDbConnection` passed around, `IDbTransactionQueryProvider` instead of `IDbTransaction`, and values bound as parameters instead of quoted into SQL. Apps that do not run code rules are not affected; no new dependency.\n- No functional changes: the code follows the repository's code rules (formatting only).\n- Package metadata: the repository url points to the git repository, the debugger steps into the sources (SourceLink, symbol package .snupkg), and these release notes are shown on NuGet. Authors and company are Siemens AG, every package has its own description and tags.",
